# Native Model Network — example btxd settings
#
# Copy into your datadir and include from btx.conf, e.g.:
#   includeconf=modelnet.conf
#
# If the btx-modeld helper binary is present, btxd starts and supervises it by
# default (modelnet=1). btxd looks for it next to itself and in libexec/;
# modelhelper=<path> names another path. Without the binary, btxd logs
# "btx-modeld not found next to btxd" and runs without the helper (with
# modelnetrequired=1 it refuses to start instead). If the helper dies, model
# RPCs fail closed and monetary consensus continues. To run the helper
# yourself, set modelrpcsocket=<path>; btxd then connects to that socket and
# does not spawn or kill the helper.
#
# With the model network on, btxd also starts the swarm observer in this
# process. There is no separate swarm program to launch.
#
# The helper btxd starts listens on port 29447 on all interfaces unless
# modelbind (below) or modelnet=0 says otherwise.
#
# Product contract: inference is local after acquire; automatic spend default 0;
# FREE_ONLY never becomes paid because a timer expired. Not a remote inference
# marketplace.

# The model network is on by default. modelnet=0 turns the helper off.
# modelnet=1

# PQ1 listen address of the helper btxd starts (default: port 29447 on all
# interfaces). 0, off or none keeps the helper on its unix RPC socket; if
# hosting is on (modelhost or modelprofile), it then listens on loopback
# port 29447 only.
# modelbind=<ip:port>
# modelbind=0

# A model-plane contact to start from (repeatable; not monetary addnode).
# No model contact is compiled in.
# modelpeer=<host:port>

# Unix JSON-RPC socket (default: <datadir>/modelnet/modeld.sock). Set it only
# for a helper you run yourself; btxd then does not start one.
# modelrpcsocket=<path>

# Optional introduction hints (require modelnet=1; not monetary AddrMan):
# modelrelay=1
# modelhost=1

# --- btx-modeld run by hand (only with modelrpcsocket=<path> set above) ---
# build/bin/btx-modeld \
#   -modeldir=<datadir>/modelnet \
#   -modelstorage=80GiB \
#   -modelseed=auto \
#   -modeltransport=pq1 \
#   -modelrpcsocket=<datadir>/modelnet/modeld.sock \
#   -modelpeer=<host:port>   # optional; repeatable; not monetary addnode
#   # -modelpreserverare     # optional unsolicited rare fetch into spare quota
#
# On OpenSSL 3.0.x hosts, use contrib/modelnet/run-modeld.sh and/or BTX_OPENSSL.
